  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation on Migration and Partnership to Achieve Sustainable Solutions (COMPASS) 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cooperation on Migration and Partnerships to Achieve Sustainable Solutions (COMPASS) was established in 2021 and is a multiyear comprehensive protection pro achieve long-term results in three interconnected outcome areas to contribute to migration governance systems, multistakeholder cooperation, and services that facilitate safe, orderly, and regular migration as well as protect and uphold the rights of migrants. The programme will focus on systemic changes that are critical to: addressing the underlying causes of migrants&#x2019; vulnerability, gender inequality and exclusion, including in humanitarian and fragile settings; supporting rights-based policies and legislation; equitable access to essential protection services; strengthening local partnerships for migrant inclusion and social cohesion; reinforcing data-driven responses; and influencing social behaviors and norms. COMPASS 2.0 contributes to IOM&#x2019;s overarching goal to ensure the protection, respect and fulfillment of the rights and well-being of migrants, regardless of their migration status and is in line with Objective 1 of the new IOM&#x2019;s Strategic Plan 2024-2028. The programme is designed to be flexible and adaptable with the aim of becoming more responsive, inclusive, and fit for purpose through increased alignment with the diversity of global, regional, and national development agenda/strategies and effectively respond to emerging challenges. COMPASS 2.0 supports IOM&#x2019;s protection programming in 14 countries (Afghanistan, Algeria, Chad, Egypt, Ethiopia, Iraq, Lebanon, Libya, Mali, Morocco, Niger, Nigeria, Sudan, and Tunisia).</narrative>
  </description>
